# Adrift settings. Copy this file to .env.local and edit what you need.
# Every variable is optional; the defaults suit one machine running both
# Adrift and ComfyUI. Restart `npm run dev` after a change (Next.js reads
# env files at startup).

# ── ComfyUI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your ComfyUI folder (the one with main.py). Adrift reads models, saved
# workflows and outputs from here. Default: ../ComfyUI next to this folder.
# Older names still work in the scripts: COMFY_DIR (start-comfyui.sh) and
# --comfy (fetch-models.mjs).
# COMFY_ROOT=/path/to/ComfyUI

# ComfyUI's HTTP address, used by the Adrift server.
# Default http://127.0.0.1:8188. Set it to override the address saved by the
# setup wizard (an active value here wins over the wizard).
# COMFY_HTTP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8188

# ComfyUI's WebSocket address, used by the browser for live progress.
# ComfyUI 0.24+ rejects a WebSocket from another port unless it was started
# with --enable-cors-header http://localhost:3000 (scripts/start-comfyui.sh
# does this for you).
# Default: the page host on port 8188.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COMFY_WS_BASE=ws://127.0.0.1:8188

# Server-side WebSocket address for the progress proxy. Default: ws://127.0.0.1:8188
# COMFY_WS_BASE=ws://127.0.0.1:8188

# Bearer token for a ComfyUI behind an auth-checking reverse proxy.
# Server-side only: every server->ComfyUI HTTP call (via comfyFetch) sends
# "Authorization: Bearer <token>"; it is never logged or sent to the browser.
# Named COMFY_BEARER (not COMFY_API_KEY) to avoid confusion with the
# comfy.org API-node key. LIMITATION: the browser's direct ComfyUI WebSocket
# (NEXT_PUBLIC_COMFY_WS_BASE) cannot carry this token — the proxy must allow
# /ws without it (e.g. LAN-only) or ComfyUI must stay on a trusted network.
# COMFY_BEARER=

# ComfyUI output folder that the admin cleanup scans. Default: ../ComfyUI/output
# COMFYUI_OUTPUT_DIR=/path/to/ComfyUI/output

# Checkpoint the Create page uses when the graph names none. Default: the
# first checkpoint ComfyUI lists. With the Starter models, set:
# COMFY_DEFAULT_CHECKPOINT=sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors

# ── Network and access ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Adrift listens on 127.0.0.1 (this computer only) by default. To open it to
# other devices (a phone on your Wi-Fi, another PC), set CJ_HOST to 0.0.0.0
# or a LAN address. A non-loopback CJ_HOST REQUIRES ADMIN_API_KEY: the server
# refuses to start without it. Never expose Adrift or ComfyUI to the internet.
# CJ_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Admin key for every API route (a long random string, e.g. the output of
# `openssl rand -hex 32`). Unset = no login; fine only while CJ_HOST is
# loopback.
# ADMIN_API_KEY=

# Session signing secret. Default: ADMIN_API_KEY.
# SESSION_SECRET=

# With ADMIN_API_KEY unset, only localhost, IP-literal and *.local Host names
# are served (DNS-rebinding guard). List extra hostnames here, comma
# separated ("*" disables the guard).
# CJ_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# Extra exact origins allowed to call the API cross-origin (CORS). The
# origin of COMFY_HTTP_URL is always allowed; add another spelling of the
# same ComfyUI here, e.g. http://localhost:8188. Nothing else is allowed.
# CJ_COMFY_ORIGINS=

# Set to 1 only when Adrift runs behind a reverse proxy you control that sets
# X-Forwarded-For. Rate limits then key on the address that proxy saw;
# otherwise X-Forwarded-For is ignored (it can be forged).
# TRUST_PROXY=

# Extra ComfyUI origins allowed to frame Adrift (the overlay inside ComfyUI).
# :8188 and :8000 on localhost are allowed by default. Space separated.
# CJ_FRAME_ANCESTORS=http://localhost:9999

# The URL you open Adrift on. The helper ComfyUI that Adrift starts for the
# optional MiniMax H3 pack, and scripts/start-comfyui.sh, pass it to
# --enable-cors-header. Default: http://localhost:3000
# CJ_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# App port. `npm run dev -- -p 3001` sets it too; also used for Bonjour and
# style preview self-links. Default: 3000
# PORT=3000

# ── Create page engines ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional image engines for the Create page. Each one stays hidden until its
# flag is set; download its weights first, then set it to 1. (The Tools page
# edit tools that use these models do not need the flag.)
# Qwen-Image 2.1 (non-commercial license), MOSS-Image. FLUX.3 Klein is on by
# default; CJ_FLUX3=0 hides it.
# CJ_QWEN_IMAGE_21=1
# CJ_FLUX3=0
# CJ_MOSS_IMAGE=1

# Optional: engine used when no model is picked (default: krea2, Krea 2).
# Also read by the browser bundle, so restart the dev server after changing it.
# On 8 GB GPUs with only the SDXL starter set, use sdxl.
# CJ_DEFAULT_PACK=sdxl
# Optional: default video pack for --video when none is given
# CJ_DEFAULT_VIDEO_PACK=

# Krea 2 draft model (--draft): a faster pruned turbo diffusion model.
# Set to its file name in models/diffusion_models once you have one.
# COMFY_KREA2_DRAFT_UNET=

# ── Memory ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Low-VRAM hint: always tile the VAE decode (same as --lowvram).
# CJ_LOW_VRAM=1
# Tile the VAE decode automatically above this many output pixels.
# Default: built-in per-model threshold.
# CJ_TILED_VAE_AUTO_PIXELS=4194304

# ── Optional second ComfyUI for video ───────────────────────────────────────
# Unset = one ComfyUI runs everything (the normal setup).
# Set it to send video jobs to a second ComfyUI: another GPU machine, or on
# Apple Silicon an fp32 video-only instance started with
#   CJ_VIDEO_FP32=1 COMFY_PORT=8189 scripts/start-comfyui.sh
# The MiniMax H3 packs and the video actions listed in COMFY_VIDEO_ACTIONS
# queue on this host; image tools stay on COMFY_HTTP_URL. Adrift copies the
# input files over and fetches the results back. Live progress previews are
# not shown for jobs on this host (it is polled every ~5 s instead).
# A ComfyUI started with --listen 127.0.0.1 on another machine is not
# reachable over the LAN; tunnel it instead, e.g.:
#   ssh -N -L 8288:127.0.0.1:8188 <video-host>
# COMFY_VIDEO_HTTP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8288
#
# Outputs the video host writes are prefixed with this subfolder
# (filename_prefix "<marker>/video/..."), which is how /view requests find
# their host. Default: adrift-video
# COMFY_VIDEO_OUTPUT_SUBFOLDER=adrift-video
#
# Override the routing tables (comma separated; empty string = none).
# COMFY_VIDEO_ACTIONS=transition,character_swap,face_swap,orbit_360,camera_move
# COMFY_VIDEO_PACKS=minimax
#
# Cross-host GPU mutex (hosts that share a breaker must never compute at the
# same time). Before queuing on one host, Adrift waits until the OTHER
# host's /queue (running + pending) is empty and serializes submissions;
# the default host's group includes the H3 warm process (CJ_H3_WARM_URL).
# An unreachable host counts as idle. Default: on when COMFY_VIDEO_HTTP_URL
# is set. Only covers jobs submitted through Adrift (not ComfyUI's own UI).
# COMFY_EXCLUSIVE_BACKENDS=1
# Max wait for the other host to drain before the submit fails with 503
# (ms, default 600000 = 10 min), and the /queue poll interval (ms, default 3000).
# COMFY_EXCLUSIVE_WAIT_MS=600000
# COMFY_EXCLUSIVE_POLL_MS=3000

# Optional MiniMax H3 pack only: address of the helper ComfyUI that keeps H3
# loaded between jobs. Default: http://127.0.0.1:8189
# CJ_H3_WARM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8189

# ── Model downloads ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CivitAI browsing and downloads (Explore → Models).
# CIVITAI_API_KEY=
# CIVITAI_API_URL=https://civitai.com/api/v1
# NSFW CivitAI API base. Default: https://civitai.red/api/v1
# CIVITAI_NSFW_API_URL=https://civitai.red/api/v1

# Encrypted CivitAI key instead of the plain one above.
# CIVITAI_API_KEY_ENCRYPTED=
# SECRETS_PASSPHRASE=
# Custom salt for secret encryption (defaults to a built-in salt; changing it makes previously saved secrets unreadable)
# SECRETS_SALT=

# Hugging Face token for gated repos (read by scripts/fetch-models.mjs only;
# logging in with the `hf` CLI works too).
# HF_TOKEN=

# ── Optional style library service (services/stylevault) ───────────────────
# Map, Clusters and Images on the Styles page need this service running. Train
# uses it when it has a trainer installed, and the local trainer otherwise.
# Start it with scripts/stylevault.sh start. See docs/STYLE_LIBRARY.md.
# Where Adrift finds the service. Default: http://127.0.0.1:8000
# Leave this unset for the default address. Setting it, even to the default,
# also sends training from Datasets to the service and shows Describe and the
# auto-sort / auto-caption buttons. Unset, Datasets trains with the local
# trainer configured in Settings → Training.
# STYLEVAULT_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# Folders the Styles page may index, and LoRA training through the service may
# read (absolute paths, comma-separated). ComfyUI's output folder can always be
# indexed. Unset = other folders are refused.
# CJ_VAULT_DATASET_ROOTS=

# These three are read by the service, not by Adrift. Set them in the shell that
# runs scripts/stylevault.sh.
# Folder for the service's database, config and downloaded model.
# STYLEVAULT_HOME=
# Image embedder. Default: siglip2, downloaded on the first index.
# color-histogram needs no weights but groups images by colour only.
# STYLEVAULT_EMBEDDER=siglip2
# Folders the service may index (absolute paths, comma-separated). It refuses
# anything else, whatever Adrift allows. When unset, scripts/stylevault.sh uses
# CJ_VAULT_DATASET_ROOTS and the ComfyUI output folder.
# STYLEVAULT_ALLOWED_ROOTS=

# ── Optional add-ons (not part of this repository) ──────────────────────────
# Standalone Krea 2 FastAPI backend. Default: http://127.0.0.1:8787
# KREA2_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# External NEvo search backend for the prompt bar's NEvo menu (the menu only
# shows when this is set).
# Default: http://127.0.0.1:8791
# NEVO_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8791

# HairDeck sidecar (github.com/hyz317/HairDeck, Apache-2.0): its Gradio demo
# (`python demo/app.py --port 7860`). Unset, the Hair Cards tool shows how to
# run it. Must be loopback (tunnel with `ssh -L`) unless HAIRDECK_ALLOW_REMOTE=1.
# HAIRDECK_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7860
# HAIRDECK_ALLOW_REMOTE=1

# Optional: local Krea moodboard image library (default ~/krea-moodboards)
# KREA_MOODBOARDS_DIR=/path/to/krea-moodboards

# Folder that moodboard auto-sort may import images from. Default: your home folder.
# MOODBOARD_IMPORT_ROOT=/path/to/pictures

# Blender executable for "Open in Blender" and GLB→USDZ export of 3D runs.
# Wins over the path saved in Settings → Blender. Unset = auto-detect per platform:
# /Applications/Blender.app, ~/Applications, homebrew, /usr/bin, snap, flatpak,
# Program Files\Blender Foundation (newest first), PATH.
# BLENDER_PATH=/path/to/blender

# ── Links shown in the app (exposed to the browser) ─────────────────────────
# "Report misuse" link shown on MiniMax H3 tools (the MiniMax H3 Community
# License asks hosted services for an abuse-report channel). http(s)://,
# mailto: or a site path. Unset = /legal/h3#report.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ABUSE_REPORT_URL=mailto:abuse@example.com

# Repository URL used by the "Report this problem" link on failed tool runs.
# Unset = the link is hidden.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CJ_REPO_URL=https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>

# ── scripts/start-comfyui.sh (read by the script, not the app) ──────────────
# COMFY_PORT=8188          ComfyUI port
# COMFY_LISTEN=127.0.0.1   ComfyUI listen address
# CJ_PREVIEW_METHOD=auto   live preview method (auto, taesd, latent2rgb, none)
# CJ_CACHE_RAM=auto        GB of RAM ComfyUI keeps free (0 = ComfyUI default)
# CJ_VIDEO_FP32=1          macOS only: fp32 UNet + VAE for a video-only instance

# ── Development and testing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Log API requests in production builds too (development always logs).
# CJ_API_LOG=1

# React Scan dev overlay (loads the dev-only script from unpkg).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_REACT_SCAN=1

# Build output folder (lets two checkouts run side by side). Default: .next
# NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next
# "standalone" = self-contained server build (the Docker image uses this).
# NEXT_OUTPUT=standalone

# Run live ComfyUI integration tests.
# COMFY_LIVE_TESTS=1

# Run saved-workflow runtime compatibility tests.
# COMFY_RUNTIME_COMPAT=1

# Rewrite the golden graph fixtures (src/__tests__/golden) from the current
# builders instead of comparing against them.
# UPDATE_GOLDEN=1

# Optional: where the setup wizard saves the ComfyUI connection
# (default data/runtime_settings.json). Env vars above always win over it.
# ADRIFT_RUNTIME_SETTINGS_FILE=

# Optional: where the list of signed-in devices is kept
# (default data/sessions.json; Account Settings > Devices).
# ADRIFT_SESSIONS_FILE=

# Optional: where imported workflow tools are stored
# (default data/user_tools.json).
# ADRIFT_USER_TOOLS_FILE=

# Optional: default edit LoRA id for the grounded edit tools (Edit photo,
# Replace person, Pose character ...) when the user hasn't picked one, e.g.
# identity-edit-v2-r128. Default: identity-edit (v1.2, Krea 2 Community
# License). The v2 identity LoRAs are non-commercial (paid licence needed).
# ADRIFT_DEFAULT_EDIT_LORA=

# Optional: video editor (Edit tab) work folder for uploads, cuts and
# filmstrips (default data/video-edit). Not cleaned automatically.
# ADRIFT_VIDEO_EDIT_DIR=

# Optional: ffmpeg / ffprobe binaries for the video editor (default: PATH;
# ffprobe is looked up next to FFMPEG_PATH first).
# FFMPEG_PATH=
# FFPROBE_PATH=

# Optional: "Report a bug" link target, for forks (exposed to the browser).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ISSUES_URL=

# Optional: judge mode, a judge-only instance for a temporary contest
# preview (see src/lib/judge/). Off unless ADRIFT_JUDGE_MODE=1. Tokens are a
# comma list (16+ chars each); each judge opens /?judge=<token> once. Run it
# as its own instance on loopback; never on the admin instance.
# ADRIFT_JUDGE_MODE=
# ADRIFT_JUDGE_TOKENS=
# Runs per token (default 15), upload cap in MB (default 25), max GPU hold
# per run in ms (default 900000).
# ADRIFT_JUDGE_RUN_QUOTA=
# ADRIFT_JUDGE_UPLOAD_MB=
# ADRIFT_JUDGE_LEASE_MS=
# Quota/ownership state (default data/judge_state.json; "off" = memory only)
# and the pause file (default data/judge_paused; exists = new runs refused).
# ADRIFT_JUDGE_STATE_FILE=
# ADRIFT_JUDGE_PAUSE_FILE=
